+# N31 pure proposal and future integration contract
+
+Phase A only. Base6292fc8cffad2eec0f789e023d835ad3c1df146a. The pure helper and synthetic tests are implemented; no production import, profile, policy/Main/adapter hook, observer, runner, native auditor or GPU release has been added. Score remains Unknown. Existing source files are unchanged, so default behavior is untouched by this commit; this is not a claim that future integrated parity has been tested.
+
+## Arithmetic and action semantics
+
+`capture_dwell_proposal(base_plan, projected_outcomes, *, target, hand_quaternion_xyzw, gripper_qpos, target_recognized)` consumes the exact native64×128 archive plan and its original canonical8×3 outcome positions, native FP32/BF16 with matching dtype. Geometry snapshots are finite floating tensors converted to CPU binary64; no projection is recomputed. Normalize the observed xyzw quaternion and use its local-to-world rotation R. For each outcome j0…7 compute a=Rᵀ(target−projected_outcome[j]); the first inclusive hit is x∈[−.008,.008], z∈[−.0116,.0044], y∈[q2+.0005,q1−.0005]. No epsilon, duration parameter, surrogate score or fitted threshold is present.
+
+Clone the base. Write native gripper10=+1 at j…7; write native39…44=+0 at j+1…7. Preserve the arrival pose increment itself, earlier actions, time8…63 and every other field, including signed zeros outside edited entries. Return a candidate only if native bytes differ. Otherwise return None with an explicit reason; do not replace ordinary offspring slot15. The helper never chooses that slot itself or forces retention/execution.
+
+Missing target/proprioception, unrecognized target, negative jaw gap, no hit and no changed native content are explicit skips. Supplied malformed tensor shapes/dtypes or nonfinite values raise ValueError rather than inventing input. A recognized, complete context must also have a finite nonzero binary64 quaternion norm; nonfinite derived displacement/transform is rejected. The future caller must bind provenance and action mask, not treat this pure helper as an admission validator.
+
+Zero pose increments mean approximate dwell, not absolute physical pose locking: root's current robosuite source review finds zero rotation preserves the prior goal orientation, while zero translation sets the current measured position as goal. +1 is a repeated close command; PandaGripper applies finite-speed incremental closure, not instantaneous closure. These are interpretation limits, not changes to the specified native assignments.
+
+The source-calibrated interval does not establish that the keypoint is an object center, that a raw canonical path is executable, that future hand orientation/aperture stays fixed, or that contact/capture occurs. At j7 only one close command is changed. A useful approach can be inhibited or a wrong snapshot can trigger a harmful dwell. No activity-count, smaller-motion or proxy-geometry gate replaces task outcomes.
+
+## Concrete production interface gap and minimal future placement
+
+The current outer call `rdt_policy_steer.py:6300–6316` returns an already scored offspring batch. Mutating after it would either leave stale quality or require another score and therefore violates the protocol. This cannot be implemented by an outer assignment alone.
+
+A future explicit opt-in pre-score proposal hook can preserve the frozen computation: the normal RBF rollout completes its denoiser/diversity/mask first; apply the prepared single candidate to row15 immediately before its existing score at4104–4111, and before binding final_population/rollout_final trace at4103/4156. The ordinary baseline/no-active-RBF path also scores internally at3749–3756, so the same narrow opt-in must reach that path and any existing fallback. Do not route into a different denoising algorithm to avoid that hook. All normal model and random operations still process all16 ordinary rows; only after them is row15 substituted. Initial16 at5320–5336 remains untouched. The no-survivor Q0 path reuses the returned rollout score at6478–6485; do not add full_population_rescore or accidentally duplicate auxiliary diagnostic scores.
+
+Prepare the candidate from the archive-global-best identity before each iteration, before that iteration's archive update. `qd_ed.py:648–655` defines the winner ordering; update stores its native action, source_iter and insert_sequence at603–614. Preserve normal parent allocation, ten renoise/rollout calls, descriptor/quality/archives/final selection. Replacing one slot changes the scientific candidate batch intentionally; it does not claim equal arithmetic or equal wall time. Primary176/11 and the existing Q0 auxiliary scoring/model/RBF schedule must remain unchanged, with zero added model/provider/RBF/random calls. Full production-cost equivalence is a later integration test obligation, not proved by these pure tests.
+
+## Current-decision cache and raw observation contract
+
+`_score_particles` already computes full_trajs at1919–1925 and records them at1928–1930. A future passive return/cache of that same object or an exact detached copy may capture first8 outcomes without a second projection or origin query. It must work with the recorder disabled; never read a debug artifact back into policy. Cache only canonical_initial(-1) and ten canonical_offspring calls, not auxiliary pretest or changed future rows. Keys must bind native dtype/shape/content, canonical occurrence, source iteration, current decision, provider/target and origin. At most176 canonical entries per decision are needed; discard the cache on new decision, target/provider/Stage/reset/episode. If same content has multiple occurrences, use archive provenance or demand agreeing stored projection/quality/origin; never choose a favorable occurrence.
+
+The caller must supply raw pre-decision quat/qpos and target snapshot from Main's already available observation/tracker data. Current N30 bridge atMain1645–1651/1831–1849 is an example of cached observation transport only; N31 requires its own opt-in packet with quat/qpos and does not enable N30 continuation. `LiberoAdapter.get_obs()` at1787–1791 returns _last_obs. **Do not use `_get_raw_obs()` at1141–1149: it performs an extra zero-action env.step.** No model, simulator, pose query, tracker generation change or observation acquisition is added. The existing N30 packet is insufficient as-is because it transports EEF position, not the required quat/qpos.
+
+The raw canonical projection originates from controller.ee_pos, whereas Main's observed position is grip_site. Keep source_origin, cast_origin and observed pose separately identified. No equality or physical-prediction claim may be silently imposed. Frozen geometry combines the original canonical positions with the current observed hand frame/aperture.
+
+## Minimal future passive evidence
+
+For each of10 proposal opportunities, record current decision/iteration, frozen archive-best source identity (cell/source_iter/insert_sequence/native fingerprint and matching canonical score/projection ref), snapshot identity, result reason/j, slot15, and native candidate identity if changed. An active event must bind original unmodified post-rollout row15, the new candidate, the actual scored batch and score reference. The other15 rows, initial population, tail/inactive fields and model/RNG call counts need independent full-path evidence. Label this a constructed capture-dwell proposal, not a model-output or exact survivor. Final selected_source strings alone do not establish survival; follow native content and occurrence identities. Record CPU copy/cache/observer overhead separately. Arithmetic and decisions must be identical with observer on/off. No such production observer is implemented in Phase A.
+
+## CPU evidence and remaining work
+
+37 distinct focused synthetic cases cover earliest/interior/last hit, exact face inclusion and one-binary64-value exclusion, rotated/scaled quaternion, negative/zero jaw gap, missing/unrecognized/no-hit, native no-change and signed-zero change, exact untouched prefix/tail/inactive fields, FP32/BF16, noncontiguous views, malformed/nonfinite input and unchanged CPU RNG. They do not run a model, scorer, environment or historical input. First invocation assertions passed but isolation failed on two blocked pycache read probes; the original log is retained. An owned empty pycache prefix fixed only the test loader boundary; the final invocation passed with zero denied accesses. No numerical helper adjustment was made to obtain those passes.
+
+Root review and a separately authorized production phase are still required for hook/capture/cache/native audit/config composition/default parity/full real call-chain tests and concrete budget/Dev release. No new hypothesis or protected evaluation is authorized by this helper commit.
